[32m+[m[32m## Installation[m
[32m+[m[32mEGM.jl is used from its source code, so that models, parsers and other parts can be added or adapted. With Julia 1.11 or later, download the repository and link it to an environment for your project:[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mgit clone https://github.com/yulanvanoppen/EGM-julia[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m```julia[m
[32m+[m[32mjulia> using Pkg[m
[32m+[m[32mjulia> Pkg.activate("path/to/MyEGMProject")               # an environment for your project[m
[32m+[m[32mjulia> Pkg.develop(path = "path/to/EGM-julia")            # use the downloaded code[m
[32m+[m[32mjulia> Pkg.add("GLMakie")                                 # optional: only for the interactive smoothing app[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mFor a complete walk-through, see [INSTALL.md](INSTALL.md). It covers Julia and the REPL, environments, the example, benchmark and test environments of the repository, changing and updating the code, and troubleshooting.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThen run the first example:[m
[32m+[m[32m```julia[m
[32m+[m[32mjulia> include("path/to/EGM-julia/examples/example.jl")[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mIt simulates noisy measurements of one state of the Higgins–Selkov oscillator, and recovers its parameters and the initial condition of the unobserved state with EGM and with trajectory matching.[m
